    "updated_at": "2026-11-14T08:33:11Z",
    "body": "Checked main (a3a59d1f6): the forward direction is already shipped by PR 1520 (commit 371db9c7c). Hovering a Geometry-tab row, its label, its remove button or any gap in the row sets State.geo_hover, and the viewport draws it with the row-hover style (ROW_HOVER_PX 3.5 over a 7 px halo, magenta, both themes) through interact::row_hover_segments. Re-ran on main and green: geo_row_hover::hovering_a_selection_row_or_its_remove_button_sets_the_hovered_selection (face, chain and vertex rows, label and remove button, cleared on leave, no command filed), geo_row_hover::row_hover_style_is_strong_and_distinct_in_both_themes, law_tests::preview_tests::row_hover_highlights_in_viewport. Left open: the reverse direction (viewport hover marks the row) is issue 1519; before/after screenshots for the PR were not attached and need a human GUI look. No code change from this run, no branch or PR. Claim released. Suggest closing this issue as already done (371db9c7c) once the maintainer has hand-checked the highlight on current main.",
